<title>RUSSIA: Russia's 364-day T-bill yields 20.00 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia's 364-day T-bill yields 20.00 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 20.00 percent at auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the average yield to be in the 19.79-19.97 percent range.</p>
<p>Series 21077 bills, maturing on June 24, 1998, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed on Tuesday at 83.97 to yield 19.77 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		   21078</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    9.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		 10.81 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		     8.97 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold				8.36 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			  6.97 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price		  83.37 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	83.25 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		  20.00 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield     20.18 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			    364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		  July 1, 1998</p>
<p>On July 2 the Finance Ministry has raised 906.22 billion roubles by selling an additional 704-day OFZ interest-bearing bond taking total proceeds from today's auctions to 7.87 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>It has also repaid 8.29 trillion roubles in a maturing 203-day T-bills (series 22062).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
